    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. Here's a summary of the changes I made to replace the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel`:\n\n**1. `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` schema (string enum GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE) with `membershipLevel`: an integer, `minimum: 1`, `maximum: 3`, `readOnly`, documented with the derivation rule. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getMembershipLevel`/`setMembershipLevel` and drops `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n**2. `OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier(owner)` mapping/method with `membershipLevel(owner)`, which computes: start at 1, +1 when an email is present, +1 when `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3.\n\n**3. `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Removed the `applyHouseholdTier` calls in `getOwner` and `addOwner` (the household-based GOLD upgrade no longer exists \u2014 the level is derived entirely from the owner's own fields, with level 4 reserved for tenure).\n- Removed the now-unused `applyHouseholdTier` method and `GOLD_HOUSEHOLD_SIZE` constant.\n- Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel` instead of the (former) tier: `Owner created: id=\u2026 customerCode=\u2026 registrationDate=\u2026 membershipLevel=\u2026`.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreNumericLevel` (unique name + email \u2192 level 3, capped) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nNote: `householdId` is still assigned on create and remains in the response \u2014 only its role in deriving the membership tier was removed, since the new spec defines the level purely from email presence and `namesakeCount`.",
